====================================================================================================
C1. 1 - h(pi(odd)) <= sum_merge (a+b) h(a/(a+b)) <= pi(R u R*) <= pi(odd) checked on 150 closed classes of random strategies (q in {3,5,7,9,11}, k = 4..9); smallest pi(odd) seen 0.3333: OK
C1b. the max-halving (greedy) strategy has stationary odd frequency 1/3 (to 1e-6) for q = 5, 7, 9 at k = 8, 10, 12 (9 closed classes)
C2. universal floor: p0 = root of p + h(p) = 1 in (0,1/2) lies in [0.227092195219348, 0.227092195219348]; every stationary law of every strategy has pi(odd) >= p0, hence rho_max >= p0 (sandwich)
    => class (i) is EMPTY at every level for every odd q >= 23 (log_q 2 <= log_23 2 = 0.22106 < p0); q = 21 (log_21 2 = 0.22767) is not covered by this bound
